WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:07.040
Speaker 1: I told you yesterday on the show
that the Tucker Carlson hour on Fox News lost

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:12.610
about half of its audience in the week after
Tucker Carlson's firing.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.980
Not hugely surprising.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.599
People are tuning in for Tucker, right?

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:20.510
I mean, when I go on vacation, we lose about
50% of our audience as well.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:26.460
The funny thing is that every guest host that
they seem to try over there seems to just

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.259
go worse and worse and worse.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:31.310
This one is really funny.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:36.320
Yesterday, the latest attempt at Tucker's
replacement is a guy named Lawrence Jones,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.080
who's worked at Fox News for some period of
time.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.100
He arguably did the worst job of anybody so
far.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.700
He interviewed Asa Hutchinson.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.449
Asa Hutchinson is a Republican candidate.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.270
He's a former Republican governor, Republican
candidate for president for the Republican

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.270
nomination.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.960
His campaign is totally dead on arrival.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.490
But they interviewed him anyway.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.490
Fine.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.800
The interview lasted eight and a half minutes.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.350
The interviewer, Lawrence Jones, spoke about
half of that time, more than four of the eight

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.350
and a half minutes.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.610
Lawrence Jones was speaking often, yelling
over Asa Hutchinson.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.640
And he tried the Why are you running?

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.060
Sort of gotcha.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.520
And when he's saw I mean, listen, I think
the policies are stupid and they're bad policies.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:23.299
But Asa Hutchinson is naming the things he
did as governor, which Republicans generally

00:01:23.299 --> 00:01:24.409
do like.

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:28.890
And Jones tries to short circuit it by saying
every Republican does that stuff.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.650
And it's sort of like, well, what do you want
me to say?

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.280
I did the things Republicans like.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:36.450
Listen to this humiliating attempt at an interview.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.630
Speaker 2: Oh, this is fair.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.659
That that is spin.

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:43.700
The Republicans have said what their position
is.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.409
I understand that you are for free speech
and all of these other issues.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:50.150
And like I said, respectfully, sir, I understand
it.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.960
You're for economic freedom and all that.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.369
Those are the typical Republican positions,
and that would work.

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:58.070
Back in 2008 or even 2006.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.600
But there there's a different Republican Party
now.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.219
And when I ask you the question, why are you
running?

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:08.860
It seems like you're opposed to all of the
things that the modern day Republican Party

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.080
stands for.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.880
What do you say to that?

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.300
Well, I disagree with that.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.000
I lowered taxes in Arkansas.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.150
That's a real solution.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.060
Republicans created surpluses.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.989
Lawrence, Lawrence, Lawrence, you've got to
listen to me as well.

00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:25.220
You've got to listen as well.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.410
We balanced the budget.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.330
That's what Republicans do.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.490
We lead in this country.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:33.750
Speaker 1: Yeah, but did you make fun of a
disabled reporter?

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:39.349
Do you pretend do you do you pretend weight
lift to attack trans people during your rallies?

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:40.800
That's what the party wants now.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.489
Speaker 2: Conservative principles.

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:47.470
And whenever you're looking at our values,
I stand second to none in terms of fighting

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.680
for pro-life values and conservative values.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.680
Look at my record, Lawrence Governor, and
you'll see that I just went through your record

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.680
here.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.769
And as I said, and I gave you credit for the
normal Republican positions.

00:02:58.769 --> 00:02:59.860
You're right in line.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.099
But this is a new Republican Party.

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:03.520
Thank you so much for your time, sir.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.820
Speaker 1: All right.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.940
Not exactly a conversation.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:15.330
I believe that the search continues for a
replacement for Tucker Carlson on Fox News.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.220
If you're curious, you can check out that
that entire interview.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:24.030
The good news for Lawrence Jones is almost
no one is watching Fox in that timeslot anymore.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.210
So not that many people saw him humiliate
himself.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.420
It's hard to determine who's less ready for
prime time.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.540
Lawrence Jones or Ron DeSantis.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:38.379
And what he did is he wanted to impress, I
guess, his bosses.

00:03:38.379 --> 00:03:42.200
So he came out ready to fight because fight
is good.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.680
But when you just talk over your guest and
you speak for half of the interview, when

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.920
you're supposed to be hearing the ideas of
the other person, it just doesn't really work

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.370
very well.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.549
And I expect we'll see what the numbers look
like by the end of this week.

00:03:55.549 --> 00:04:00.920
I expect that this week's Tucker ratings,
the former lead Tucker ratings will be even

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.250
worse than last week.

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.420
So Fox News certainly has some problems on
its hands.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.230
I'm not too worried about helping them solve
those problems.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:12.689
And if you're curious what this interview
look like, we'll have the clip on our Instagram,

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:16.130
which you can find by searching Instagram
for David Pakman show.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.979
We're going to take a quick break.

00:04:17.979 --> 00:05:15.110
So much more to discuss 

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:35.139
with 

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:40.909
you today.

